    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d416">

                <pb facs="0518" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.3227/7–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-18T22:00:00-04:00">July 18, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2210. On June 24 the Department, through an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> to the Brazilian Embassy,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d416-f1"
                    /> invited the Brazilian Government to participate in informal exploratory talks
                    on post-war civil aviation. To date no reply has been received.</p>
                <pb facs="0519" n="509" xml:id="pg509"/>
                <p>Anything that you can discreetly and informally do to expedite acceptance of this
                    invitation and the commencement of the talks at an early date will be
                        helpful.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d416-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d416-f1" n="53" xml:id="d416-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 35, <ref target="#pg494">p. 494</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d416-f2" n="54" xml:id="d416-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Caffery in telegram 2826, August 9, 1944, reported that he had, on the
                    previous day, made inquiries of the Brazilian Minister of Air, who stated that
                    his principal officers had under study the proposed exploratory talks on postwar
                    civil aviation (711.3227/8–944).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
